{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790010215,"nonce":"Mh9MPK9mA5uEcabMQVqrgo26NC0=","message":"Scope note from the schema design (2026-09-21): one repository is one project, matching the Jira bridge's existing 'one bridge = one project' assumption. No project dimension is threaded through fields, queries and UIs.\n\nSo this story's 'cross-project' is aggregation across several stores, not a project column inside one — which is a different design than the title implies, and worth confronting when it starts rather than discovering mid-build. The alternative (a project dimension in the schema) was considered and deliberately deferred to here: if aggregation turns out to be the wrong shape, this is the story that reopens it.","files":null}]}